  "source_text_hash": "cf1248efd6bc139db2a46ae6352f0429a024ddf750e1c42a986ecdf3124d9f6b",
  "transcript": [
    "You have left employment, but that does not automatically make you free. Freedom is not the absence of a manager. It is the ability to decide what deserves your time, then having the discipline to honour that decision.",
    "When somebody else controlled your calendar, wasted hours were partly their responsibility. Now they are entirely yours. That is the privilege. It is also the burden.",
    "Give your days structure before the world gives them distraction. Decide when you work. Decide when you train. Decide when you think. Decide when you stop. Protect long, uninterrupted hours for difficult work. Leave enough space to remain human.",
    "A calendar is not merely a schedule. It is a record of what you believe matters. If your stated values and your actual time do not agree, trust the calendar.",
    "You finally own your day. Treat it as something valuable."
  ],
